KG42.register("nodes-65c7b3e4c480b27c972e14b2",{"id":"COMP-89ca1857e29bb0c7","code":"PRC035","label":"Pricing at the intersection of supply and demand bid curves","definition":"In the local double-sided electric energy auction, supply offers are ordered ascending and demand offers descending to form supply and demand curves, and the price coordinate of the intersection determines the market clearing price.","layer":"L6","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"pricing.local","concept_ids":["pricing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"definition":"In the local double-sided electric energy auction, supply offers are ordered ascending and demand offers descending to form supply and demand curves, and the price coordinate of the intersection determines the market clearing price.","object":"The supply-demand price-quantity curves of local electric energy trading and the market price corresponding to their intersection.","inputs":"Bids and corresponding quantities of buyer demand and seller supply; the sources of quantities and detailed curve-construction rules are retained in the respective members.","operation":"Sort separately by buyer and seller role to construct supply and demand curves, locate the intersection, and take its price coordinate.","outputs":"Local market clearing price; the applicable price scope of each member is retained separately.","boundary":"Limited to intersection pricing within L6 and the DA template. Quantity dispatch, optimization objectives, trading permission, price publication, and settlement do not become parent operations; no rules are added for the case where the intersection does not exist or is not unique, and the same-round uniform price commitment for all accepted buy and sell bids in 45 is not generalized to 33."},"exclusions":[["Day-ahead forward double-sided auction, in which the MO calculates prices for H-MGs and retailers.","Quantities come from the Nash equilibrium optimal dispatch in Step 4; prices come from the supply and demand bids submitted by participants.","Aggregate supply and demand are monotonically increasing and decreasing step curves, respectively.","The MCP is used for surplus-electricity trading and calculation of participant revenues; the retailer purchases, at the MCP, surplus electricity not sold to other H-MGs."],["The MO organizes supply and demand bids with the objective of maximizing social welfare; this objective is not equated with the Nash-equilibrium quantity source of 33.","In the same clearing round, all accepted bids pay or receive the same market price; the price may vary across rounds.","The market price is communicated to each agent and used for settlement of electric energy charges; taxes, network charges, and deviation charges still belong to other cost components.","A buyer bid not below the market price and a seller bid not above the market price respectively constitute buy and sell permission conditions, and cannot replace the intersection-pricing definition.","The price increase driven by synchronized heat-pump demand bids is an observation for a specific scenario; no detailed price-selection rule is given for the case of a non-unique intersection."]],"members":[{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The local MCP informs the H-MG's sale of excess power to other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. Condition: The H-MG has excess generation after satisfying its local demand. Retailers purchase the remaining H-MG excess power at the local MCP. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Condition: The H-MG's excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs. A H-MG with a power shortage may purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG purchases from other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed retail market. Condition: The H-MG has a power shortage. This exchange capability requires an energy management system for decision-making in day-ahead and real-time operation. Scope: Energy exchange among adjacent H-MGs connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform. Condition: A microgrid seeks to sell excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or cover its power shortage through neighbours.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Energy exchange among adjacent H-MGs connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform. | H-MG purchases from other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed retail market. | H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. | Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"]},"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"a373f2494dedf05bb99efa8cb9166e898fbb8dbf3dd81d563e2d1a99025e20f3","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","market_meaning":"Submitted demand bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. Submitted supply bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. The optimal participant allocations obtained through Nash-equilibrium scheduling are inputs to the local MCP calculation. Scope: Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction. The market operator calculates the optimum local market price using information received from buyers and sellers. Scope: Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers. The MCP is set at the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Scope: Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction. | Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. | Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction. | Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"]},"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C005"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"01edbe4a8a90803249e111c22e444459438fa4908c79e602030e587febeb904f","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","market_meaning":"The MCP sets the monetary price payable by retailers for H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs in the proposed retail market. Condition: H-MG excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs in the proposed retail market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"]},"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"ae55fb0b9e84a0440938ffee573357095657615044b2f067bbb96b6327ba619b","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Demand submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. Supply submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. Demand submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. Supply submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. The local market operator coordinates clearing by ensuring balance between total accepted consumption and generation. Scope: Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. Buyers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a purchase allocation. Scope: Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a sale allocation. Scope: Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The seller's offer price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM clears every 15 min with a 24 h trading horizon. Scope: Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. Local clearing must balance total accepted demand and total accepted supply. Scope: The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. | Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. | Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities. | The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C006","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C007"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1a48a3ca7bf338b63c7eadeda4cf87b884cede3824a558f1a1e72f6dcbf1df91","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The local market closing price is communicated to each agent as the participant price signal. Scope: Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"6b91536757ffe4e2c8555ab4f9ecced95fd4cfe9eba05a1e93d50abd6ae594ce","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Demand bids are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Supply offers are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Local market clearing occurs before the physical energy exchange at the delivery time step. Scope: Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. Buyers may purchase energy when their bid price meets or exceeds the uniform local market price. Scope: Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers may sell energy when their offered price does not exceed the uniform local market price. Scope: Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The seller's offered price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM permits electricity trading up to 24 h in advance of delivery. Scope: Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. | Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation. | Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. | Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C004","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C005"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"8625e846a0dbcb8eacf18cc908b4bf6523c5cea0eecea164bf38bfdf4df4269a","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"Buyers meeting the stated local-market-price threshold are permitted to buy. Scope: Buyer selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. Condition: The buyer bids at or above the uniform local market price. Sellers meeting the stated local-market-price threshold are permitted to sell. Scope: Seller selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. Condition: The seller's selling price is at or below the uniform local market price. The retailer is placed at the end of trading priority, selling at a high price or purchasing excess energy at a low price. Scope: Retailer trading priority in the study's double-sided auction. Condition: The retailer acts as a seller or buyer to balance the market. The retailer is the required buyer of this excess PV energy at a fixed rate of 1 cent/kWh; the source states that this applies regardless of the presence of LEMs. Scope: The reported excess-PV situation, including its LEM case; this is not generalized to all PV sales. Condition: PV energy is excess in the situation described by the source.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"Buyer selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. | Retailer trading priority in the study's double-sided auction. | Seller selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. | The reported excess-PV situation, including its LEM case; this is not generalized to all PV sales.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g03-E14"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002"],"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","source_rule_sha256":"227f54d009b16e3b532e6173aa3a642eb4bbf2f868784f217b220543d2aa2a71","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","market_meaning":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. In the reported transition-time case, synchronized demand-bid submissions for the same delivery time cause an increase in local market clearing prices. Scope: Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM. Condition: Multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously and submit bids for the same delivery time. The local auction uses uniform pricing. Scope: Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. | Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction. | Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C002","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C003"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"8bf8f0ca152c3dc6cfa5233cf8b0b1b2ff52401389fa0044f1cb7ab2545a0592","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R013","market_meaning":"The local market clearing price is used for energy-cost settlement; accepted bids in a clearing round pay or receive the same market price. Scope: Accepted bids in each uniform-price LEM clearing round. Condition: The bid is accepted in the relevant clearing round. Electricity delivery precedes settlement of consumption or generation, which occurs soon after delivery. Scope: Electricity delivery and subsequent settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. Final costs are settled using metering data reflecting real consumption. Scope: Final cost settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. Prosumer costs comprise LEM energy costs, levies, and balancing costs; levies comprise taxes and network charges. Scope: Cost components for participants termed prosumers in the study. Deviation from the traded position incurs additional balancing costs during settlement. Scope: Imbalance charging during LEM settlement. Condition: A prosumer's consumption or generation does not align with the bids accepted by the LEM. The proposed measure charges prosumers additional costs according to their peak loads during one day. Scope: The study's proposed additional daily-demand-charge measure. Condition: The proposed daily demand charges are applied.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Accepted bids in each uniform-price LEM clearing round. | Cost components for participants termed prosumers in the study. | Electricity delivery and subsequent settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. | Final cost settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. | Imbalance charging during LEM settlement. | The study's proposed additional daily-demand-charge measure.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e16"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013::v141-c-R013-C001"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"5e919c8e614d688cf25f6801f2b8c485c5feb3077f68c7d102652e598c548a3c","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["33-retail_market_interoperability","45-heat_pump_flexibility"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Interoperability of the H-MGs is yet another feature of the proposed market. When a H-MG comes across excess generation, after satisfying its local demand, it tends to sell excess power to other H-MGs or retailers in the market based on the MCP. Alternatively, a H-MG with power shortage can purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers.","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Interoperability of the H-MGs is yet another feature of the proposed market. When a H-MG comes across excess generation, after satisfying its local demand, it tends to sell excess power to other H-MGs or retailers in the market based on the MCP. Alternatively, a H-MG with power shortage can purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48].","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"upfront cost of required devices to participate in the market for each H-MG, which encourages more p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"From Step 2, the shortage and excess power of each H-MG is known for every scenario without considering the retailers and interoperability among H-MGs. In Step 3, however, a scheduling problem is solved (in the PBUC unit) in the presence of participating retailers and power shortage/surplus of each H-MG. As it is shown in Fig. 3, each retailer participates in the market by submitting two separate sets of bids: bid-in demand for purchasing excess power from H-MGs, and bid-in supply for selling power to support H-MGs with power shortage. Bids are submitted in the form of blocks of price and energy quantity. Step 3 also determines the upper limit for sold/purchased power to/from each retailer while maximizing exploitation of the H-MG generation. Further details are given in Section 4.","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"From Step 2, the shortage and excess power of each H-MG is known for every scenario without considering the retailers and interoperability among H-MGs. In Step 3, however, a scheduling problem is solved (in the PBUC unit) in the presence of participating retailers and power shortage/surplus of each H-MG. As it is shown in Fig. 3, each retailer participates in the market by submitting two separate sets of bids: bid-in demand for purchasing excess power from H-MGs, and bid-in supply for selling power to support H-MGs with power shortage. Bids are submitted in the form of blocks of price and energy quantity. Step 3 also determines the upper limit for sold/purchased power to/from each retailer while maximizing exploitation of the H-MG generation. Further details are given in Section 4."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"6. MCP unit","anchor_text":"by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auc- ess tion [52]. The forward marke","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]. The forward market aggregates the supply and demand in the merit order in terms of price-quantity pairs. The quantities are optimal schedules obtained from Step 4, and the prices are supply and demand bids submitted by the players. As expected, the aggregated supply and demand quantity-price values are monotonically increasing and decreasing step-wise curves, respectively. MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Finally, the pay-off function will be computed for each player based on the MCP.","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]. The forward market aggregates the supply and demand in the merit order in terms of price-quantity pairs. The quantities are optimal schedules obtained from Step 4, and the prices are supply and demand bids submitted by the players. As expected, the aggregated supply and demand quantity-price values are monotonically increasing and decreasing step-wise curves, respectively. MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Finally, the pay-off function will be computed for each player based on the MCP."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"a single H-MG can have both generator and consumer as players in the market. This feature is preferr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market operator (MO) is the entity who manages the retail market and its participants. The MO could be either a separate entity overseen by the distribution network operator (DNO) or the distribution management system (DMS) or a part of existing distribution system operator (DSO)/DMS which alternatively becomes a flexible DSO. In any case, the functionalities of the proposed market structure will remain the same. The optimum price is calculated by the MO using information received from buyers and sellers.","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"The market operator (MO) is the entity who manages the retail market and its participants. The MO could be either a separate entity overseen by the distribution network operator (DNO) or the distribution management system (DMS) or a part of existing distribution system operator (DSO)/DMS which alternatively becomes a flexible DSO. In any case, the functionalities of the proposed market structure will remain the same. The optimum price is calculated by the MO using information received from buyers and sellers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48].","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","quote":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a so ute educt o o t e e e gy su p us s a ecause o t e lower solar radiation in winter. cl The compa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"LEMs aim to provide advantageous electricity prices by facilitating lower local market prices for all participants. Energy buyers can save costs by using electricity cheaper than the retailer prices, while energy sellers can earn more money compared to direct sales to the retailer. These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","quote":"LEMs aim to provide advantageous electricity prices by facilitating lower local market prices for all participants. Energy buyers can save costs by using electricity cheaper than the retailer prices, while energy sellers can earn more money compared to direct sales to the retailer. These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"e pp y p gy, clearing prices in the LEM fluctuate in day time. It can be observed at that it drops s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Although the weighted average prices at night are all identical to the retailer’s supply price due to the lack of renewable energy, the market clearing prices in the LEM fluctuate in day time. It can be observed that it drops significantly once PV generation is abundant in transition time and summer. In summer, most bids are cleared at 1 cent/kWh in the middle of the day because of the sufficient supply of PV power and the lack of heat demand. In contrast, the market clearing prices in transition time fluctuate strongly. This stems from the diverse operation schedules of heat pumps. Once multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously, they submit their bids in the LEM for the same delivery time, causing the increase in market clearing prices. When there is no heat demand, the market clearing prices drop to a low level. In winter, the situation is totally different. Owing to the high heat demand and low supply of PV power, electricity prices are always cleared at a high level. Even though some trading is completed at 5–6 cents/kWh, most are at 10 cents/kWh. Therefore, the cost-saving potential of the LEM for prosumers in winter is not obvious.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","quote":"Although the weighted average prices at night are all identical to the retailer’s supply price due to the lack of renewable energy, the market clearing prices in the LEM fluctuate in day time. It can be observed that it drops significantly once PV generation is abundant in transition time and summer. In summer, most bids are cleared at 1 cent/kWh in the middle of the day because of the sufficient supply of PV power and the lack of heat demand. In contrast, the market clearing prices in transition time fluctuate strongly. This stems from the diverse operation schedules of heat pumps. Once multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously, they submit their bids in the LEM for the same delivery time, causing the increase in market clearing prices. When there is no heat demand, the market clearing prices drop to a low level. In winter, the situation is totally different. Owing to the high heat demand and low supply of PV power, electricity prices are always cleared at a high level. Even though some trading is completed at 5–6 cents/kWh, most are at 10 cents/kWh. Therefore, the cost-saving potential of the LEM for prosumers in winter is not obvious."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","quote":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R013","quote":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The cost for prosumers consists of three components: energy costs By from the LEM, levies, and balan","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 3","image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The cost for prosumers consists of three components: energy costs from the LEM, levies, and balancing costs. The energy costs are settled based on the market clearing price in the LEM, which changes with each clearing round. Levies refer to taxes and network charges, while balancing cost is incurred when a prosumer’s consumption or generation does not align with the bids accepted by the LEM. The retailer price refers to the bid prices of the retailer. Information about the pricing parameters is summarized in Table 3. The (+) symbol indicates when prosumers are importing energy, and the (−) symbol indicates when they are exporting energy.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R013","quote":"The cost for prosumers consists of three components: energy costs from the LEM, levies, and balancing costs. The energy costs are settled based on the market clearing price in the LEM, which changes with each clearing round. Levies refer to taxes and network charges, while balancing cost is incurred when a prosumer’s consumption or generation does not align with the bids accepted by the LEM. The retailer price refers to the bid prices of the retailer. Information about the pricing parameters is summarized in Table 3. The (+) symbol indicates when prosumers are importing energy, and the (−) symbol indicates when they are exporting energy."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["aggregate_bid_curve_intersection_price","uniform_auction_clearing_price"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L6-e13de80226","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L6","ontological_kind":"aggregate_bid_curve_intersection_price"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"In the local double-sided electric energy auction, supply offers are ordered ascending and demand offers descending to form supply and demand curves, and the price coordinate of the intersection determines the market clearing price.","object":"The supply-demand price-quantity curves of local electric energy trading and the market price corresponding to their intersection.","inputs":"Bids and corresponding quantities of buyer demand and seller supply; the sources of quantities and detailed curve-construction rules are retained in the respective members.","operation":"Sort separately by buyer and seller role to construct supply and demand curves, locate the intersection, and take its price coordinate.","outputs":"Local market clearing price; the applicable price scope of each member is retained separately.","boundary":"Limited to intersection pricing within L6 and the DA template. Quantity dispatch, optimization objectives, trading permission, price publication, and settlement do not become parent operations; no rules are added for the case where the intersection does not exist or is not unique, and the same-round uniform price commitment for all accepted buy and sell bids in 45 is not generalized to 33."},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","paper_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The local MCP informs the H-MG's sale of excess power to other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. Condition: The H-MG has excess generation after satisfying its local demand. Retailers purchase the remaining H-MG excess power at the local MCP. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Condition: The H-MG's excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs. A H-MG with a power shortage may purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG purchases from other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed retail market. Condition: The H-MG has a power shortage. This exchange capability requires an energy management system for decision-making in day-ahead and real-time operation. Scope: Energy exchange among adjacent H-MGs connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform. Condition: A microgrid seeks to sell excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or cover its power shortage through neighbours.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Energy exchange among adjacent H-MGs connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform. | H-MG purchases from other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed retail market. | H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. | Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"]},"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"a373f2494dedf05bb99efa8cb9166e898fbb8dbf3dd81d563e2d1a99025e20f3"},{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","market_meaning":"Submitted demand bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. Submitted supply bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. The optimal participant allocations obtained through Nash-equilibrium scheduling are inputs to the local MCP calculation. Scope: Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction. The market operator calculates the optimum local market price using information received from buyers and sellers. Scope: Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers. The MCP is set at the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Scope: Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction. | Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. | Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction. | Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"]},"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C005"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"01edbe4a8a90803249e111c22e444459438fa4908c79e602030e587febeb904f"},{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","market_meaning":"The MCP sets the monetary price payable by retailers for H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs in the proposed retail market. Condition: H-MG excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs in the proposed retail market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"]},"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"ae55fb0b9e84a0440938ffee573357095657615044b2f067bbb96b6327ba619b"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local MCP informs the H-MG's sale of excess power to other H-MGs or retailers. Scope: H-MG sales of excess generation to other H-MGs or retailers in the proposed local retail market. Condition: The H-MG has excess generation after satisfying its local demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Interoperability of the H-MGs is yet another feature of the proposed market. When a H-MG comes across excess generation, after satisfying its local demand, it tends to sell excess power to other H-MGs or retailers in the market based on the MCP. Alternatively, a H-MG with power shortage can purchase the cheapest available energy from other H-MGs or retailers."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Retailers purchase the remaining H-MG excess power at the local MCP. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Condition: The H-MG's excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted demand bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"upfront cost of required devices to participate in the market for each H-MG, which encourages more p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"From Step 2, the shortage and excess power of each H-MG is known for every scenario without considering the retailers and interoperability among H-MGs. In Step 3, however, a scheduling problem is solved (in the PBUC unit) in the presence of participating retailers and power shortage/surplus of each H-MG. As it is shown in Fig. 3, each retailer participates in the market by submitting two separate sets of bids: bid-in demand for purchasing excess power from H-MGs, and bid-in supply for selling power to support H-MGs with power shortage. Bids are submitted in the form of blocks of price and energy quantity. Step 3 also determines the upper limit for sold/purchased power to/from each retailer while maximizing exploitation of the H-MG generation. Further details are given in Section 4."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"6. MCP unit","anchor_text":"by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auc- ess tion [52]. The forward marke","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]. The forward market aggregates the supply and demand in the merit order in terms of price-quantity pairs. The quantities are optimal schedules obtained from Step 4, and the prices are supply and demand bids submitted by the players. As expected, the aggregated supply and demand quantity-price values are monotonically increasing and decreasing step-wise curves, respectively. MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Finally, the pay-off function will be computed for each player based on the MCP."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted supply bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"upfront cost of required devices to participate in the market for each H-MG, which encourages more p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"From Step 2, the shortage and excess power of each H-MG is known for every scenario without considering the retailers and interoperability among H-MGs. In Step 3, however, a scheduling problem is solved (in the PBUC unit) in the presence of participating retailers and power shortage/surplus of each H-MG. As it is shown in Fig. 3, each retailer participates in the market by submitting two separate sets of bids: bid-in demand for purchasing excess power from H-MGs, and bid-in supply for selling power to support H-MGs with power shortage. Bids are submitted in the form of blocks of price and energy quantity. Step 3 also determines the upper limit for sold/purchased power to/from each retailer while maximizing exploitation of the H-MG generation. Further details are given in Section 4."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"6. MCP unit","anchor_text":"by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auc- ess tion [52]. The forward marke","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]. The forward market aggregates the supply and demand in the merit order in terms of price-quantity pairs. The quantities are optimal schedules obtained from Step 4, and the prices are supply and demand bids submitted by the players. As expected, the aggregated supply and demand quantity-price values are monotonically increasing and decreasing step-wise curves, respectively. MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Finally, the pay-off function will be computed for each player based on the MCP."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The optimal participant allocations obtained through Nash-equilibrium scheduling are inputs to the local MCP calculation. Scope: Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e032"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"6. MCP unit","anchor_text":"by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auc- ess tion [52]. The forward marke","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]. The forward market aggregates the supply and demand in the merit order in terms of price-quantity pairs. The quantities are optimal schedules obtained from Step 4, and the prices are supply and demand bids submitted by the players. As expected, the aggregated supply and demand quantity-price values are monotonically increasing and decreasing step-wise curves, respectively. MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Finally, the pay-off function will be computed for each player based on the MCP."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The market operator calculates the optimum local market price using information received from buyers and sellers. Scope: Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"a single H-MG can have both generator and consumer as players in the market. This feature is preferr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market operator (MO) is the entity who manages the retail market and its participants. The MO could be either a separate entity overseen by the distribution network operator (DNO) or the distribution management system (DMS) or a part of existing distribution system operator (DSO)/DMS which alternatively becomes a flexible DSO. In any case, the functionalities of the proposed market structure will remain the same. The optimum price is calculated by the MO using information received from buyers and sellers."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MCP is set at the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Scope: Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e032"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"6. MCP unit","anchor_text":"by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auc- ess tion [52]. The forward marke","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]. The forward market aggregates the supply and demand in the merit order in terms of price-quantity pairs. The quantities are optimal schedules obtained from Step 4, and the prices are supply and demand bids submitted by the players. As expected, the aggregated supply and demand quantity-price values are monotonically increasing and decreasing step-wise curves, respectively. MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Finally, the pay-off function will be computed for each player based on the MCP."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MCP sets the monetary price payable by retailers for H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs. Scope: Retailer purchases of H-MG excess power remaining unsold to other H-MGs in the proposed retail market. Condition: H-MG excess power has not been sold to other H-MGs.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"],"ref":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R011","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"nication channel between H MG and MO, and to operate internal devices upon receiving schedules from ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To encourage H-MGs to participate in the market with more local generation, their excess power, which has not been sold to other H-MGs, will be purchased by retailers at the MCP [48]."}]}],"variables":[],"parameters":[]},{"unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","paper_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Demand submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. Supply submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. Demand submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. Supply submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. The local market operator coordinates clearing by ensuring balance between total accepted consumption and generation. Scope: Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. Buyers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a purchase allocation. Scope: Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a sale allocation. Scope: Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The seller's offer price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM clears every 15 min with a 24 h trading horizon. Scope: Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. Local clearing must balance total accepted demand and total accepted supply. Scope: The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. | Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. | Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities. | The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C006","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C007"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1a48a3ca7bf338b63c7eadeda4cf87b884cede3824a558f1a1e72f6dcbf1df91"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The local market closing price is communicated to each agent as the participant price signal. Scope: Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"6b91536757ffe4e2c8555ab4f9ecced95fd4cfe9eba05a1e93d50abd6ae594ce"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Demand bids are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Supply offers are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Local market clearing occurs before the physical energy exchange at the delivery time step. Scope: Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. Buyers may purchase energy when their bid price meets or exceeds the uniform local market price. Scope: Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers may sell energy when their offered price does not exceed the uniform local market price. Scope: Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The seller's offered price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM permits electricity trading up to 24 h in advance of delivery. Scope: Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. | Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation. | Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. | Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C004","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C005"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"8625e846a0dbcb8eacf18cc908b4bf6523c5cea0eecea164bf38bfdf4df4269a"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"Buyers meeting the stated local-market-price threshold are permitted to buy. Scope: Buyer selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. Condition: The buyer bids at or above the uniform local market price. Sellers meeting the stated local-market-price threshold are permitted to sell. Scope: Seller selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. Condition: The seller's selling price is at or below the uniform local market price. The retailer is placed at the end of trading priority, selling at a high price or purchasing excess energy at a low price. Scope: Retailer trading priority in the study's double-sided auction. Condition: The retailer acts as a seller or buyer to balance the market. The retailer is the required buyer of this excess PV energy at a fixed rate of 1 cent/kWh; the source states that this applies regardless of the presence of LEMs. Scope: The reported excess-PV situation, including its LEM case; this is not generalized to all PV sales. Condition: PV energy is excess in the situation described by the source.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"Buyer selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. | Retailer trading priority in the study's double-sided auction. | Seller selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. | The reported excess-PV situation, including its LEM case; this is not generalized to all PV sales.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g03-E14"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002"],"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","source_rule_sha256":"227f54d009b16e3b532e6173aa3a642eb4bbf2f868784f217b220543d2aa2a71"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","market_meaning":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. In the reported transition-time case, synchronized demand-bid submissions for the same delivery time cause an increase in local market clearing prices. Scope: Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM. Condition: Multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously and submit bids for the same delivery time. The local auction uses uniform pricing. Scope: Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. | Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction. | Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C002","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C003"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"8bf8f0ca152c3dc6cfa5233cf8b0b1b2ff52401389fa0044f1cb7ab2545a0592"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R013","market_meaning":"The local market clearing price is used for energy-cost settlement; accepted bids in a clearing round pay or receive the same market price. Scope: Accepted bids in each uniform-price LEM clearing round. Condition: The bid is accepted in the relevant clearing round. Electricity delivery precedes settlement of consumption or generation, which occurs soon after delivery. Scope: Electricity delivery and subsequent settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. Final costs are settled using metering data reflecting real consumption. Scope: Final cost settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. Prosumer costs comprise LEM energy costs, levies, and balancing costs; levies comprise taxes and network charges. Scope: Cost components for participants termed prosumers in the study. Deviation from the traded position incurs additional balancing costs during settlement. Scope: Imbalance charging during LEM settlement. Condition: A prosumer's consumption or generation does not align with the bids accepted by the LEM. The proposed measure charges prosumers additional costs according to their peak loads during one day. Scope: The study's proposed additional daily-demand-charge measure. Condition: The proposed daily demand charges are applied.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Accepted bids in each uniform-price LEM clearing round. | Cost components for participants termed prosumers in the study. | Electricity delivery and subsequent settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. | Final cost settlement in the stated LEM exchange procedure. | Imbalance charging during LEM settlement. | The study's proposed additional daily-demand-charge measure.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e16"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013::v141-c-R013-C001"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"5e919c8e614d688cf25f6801f2b8c485c5feb3077f68c7d102652e598c548a3c"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C006","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Buyers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a purchase allocation. Scope: Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price.","expression":"p_i^{bid} \\ge p^M \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\text{buyer } i \\text{ may receive a purchase allocation}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-p-market","v141-c-R003-theta-p-bid-i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C007","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Sellers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a sale allocation. Scope: Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The seller's offer price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price.","expression":"p_j^{offer} \\le p^M \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\text{seller } j \\text{ may receive a sale allocation}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-p-market","v141-c-R003-theta-p-offer-j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market closing price is communicated to each agent as the participant price signal. Scope: Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Buyers may purchase energy when their bid price meets or exceeds the uniform local market price. Scope: Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price.","expression":"\\forall i,\\; p^{bid}_i \\ge p^{market} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{buy}_i","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["p_bid_i"],"parameter_refs":["p_market"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C005","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Sellers may sell energy when their offered price does not exceed the uniform local market price. Scope: Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The seller's offered price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price.","expression":"\\forall j,\\; p^{offer}_j \\le p^{market} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{sell}_j","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["p_offer_j"],"parameter_refs":["p_market"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Buyers meeting the stated local-market-price threshold are permitted to buy. Scope: Buyer selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. Condition: The buyer bids at or above the uniform local market price.","expression":"forall i, t: p_{t,bid,i} >= p^{market}_{t} -> can_buy_{i,t}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_buyer_bid_price"],"parameter_refs":["theta_uniform_market_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Sellers meeting the stated local-market-price threshold are permitted to sell. Scope: Seller selection in the study's uniform-price double-sided auction. Condition: The seller's selling price is at or below the uniform local market price.","expression":"forall j, t: p_{t,offer,j} \u003c= p^{market}_{t} -> can_sell_{j,t}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_seller_offer_price"],"parameter_refs":["theta_uniform_market_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R011","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a so ute educt o o t e e e gy su p us s a ecause o t e lower solar radiation in winter. cl The compa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"LEMs aim to provide advantageous electricity prices by facilitating lower local market prices for all participants. Energy buyers can save costs by using electricity cheaper than the retailer prices, while energy sellers can earn more money compared to direct sales to the retailer. These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"In the reported transition-time case, synchronized demand-bid submissions for the same delivery time cause an increase in local market clearing prices. Scope: Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM. Condition: Multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously and submit bids for the same delivery time.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R011","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"e pp y p gy, clearing prices in the LEM fluctuate in day time. It can be observed at that it drops s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Although the weighted average prices at night are all identical to the retailer’s supply price due to the lack of renewable energy, the market clearing prices in the LEM fluctuate in day time. It can be observed that it drops significantly once PV generation is abundant in transition time and summer. In summer, most bids are cleared at 1 cent/kWh in the middle of the day because of the sufficient supply of PV power and the lack of heat demand. In contrast, the market clearing prices in transition time fluctuate strongly. This stems from the diverse operation schedules of heat pumps. Once multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously, they submit their bids in the LEM for the same delivery time, causing the increase in market clearing prices. When there is no heat demand, the market clearing prices drop to a low level. In winter, the situation is totally different. Owing to the high heat demand and low supply of PV power, electricity prices are always cleared at a high level. Even though some trading is completed at 5–6 cents/kWh, most are at 10 cents/kWh. Therefore, the cost-saving potential of the LEM for prosumers in winter is not obvious."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local auction uses uniform pricing. Scope: Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R011","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R013-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market clearing price is used for energy-cost settlement; accepted bids in a clearing round pay or receive the same market price. Scope: Accepted bids in each uniform-price LEM clearing round. Condition: The bid is accepted in the relevant clearing round.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g02-e16"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013::v141-c-R013-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R013","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The cost for prosumers consists of three components: energy costs By from the LEM, levies, and balan","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 3","image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The cost for prosumers consists of three components: energy costs from the LEM, levies, and balancing costs. The energy costs are settled based on the market clearing price in the LEM, which changes with each clearing round. Levies refer to taxes and network charges, while balancing cost is incurred when a prosumer’s consumption or generation does not align with the bids accepted by the LEM. The retailer price refers to the bid prices of the retailer. Information about the pricing parameters is summarized in Table 3. The (+) symbol indicates when prosumers are importing energy, and the (−) symbol indicates when they are exporting energy."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"p_bid_i","symbol":"p^{bid}_i","meaning":"Bid price submitted by buyer i in the uniform-price local auction, used in the buyer-side trading permission condition.","kind":"operational","domain":"Buyer bid-price values in the modeled LEM auction; the cited evidence does not state numeric bounds.","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::x::p_bid_i"},{"variable_id":"p_offer_j","symbol":"p^{offer}_j","meaning":"Offer price submitted by seller j in the uniform-price local auction, used in the seller-side trading permission condition.","kind":"operational","domain":"Seller offer-price values in the modeled LEM auction; the cited evidence does not state numeric bounds.","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::x::p_offer_j"},{"variable_id":"x_buyer_bid_price","symbol":"p_{t,bid,i}","meaning":"Buyer i's bid price in the modeled uniform-price double-sided auction, compared with the uniform local market price for buyer admissibility.","kind":"operational","domain":"Price values generated by the source bid-price rule p_{t,bid}=p_{max}-(t_d-t) Delta p for t_d-Delta T \u003c= t \u003c= t_d; the source gives p_max, p_min and a 6-24 h Delta T but no numeric price ceiling or floor in this rule evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["i (buyer)","t (auction time step)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::x::x_buyer_bid_price"},{"variable_id":"x_seller_offer_price","symbol":"p_{t,offer,j}","meaning":"Seller j's offer or selling price in the modeled uniform-price double-sided auction, compared with the uniform local market price for seller admissibility.","kind":"operational","domain":"Price values generated by the source offer-price rule p_{t,offer}=p_{min}+(t_d-t) Delta p for t_d-Delta T \u003c= t \u003c= t_d; the source gives p_min, p_max and a 6-24 h Delta T but no numeric price floor or ceiling in this rule evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["j (seller)","t (auction time step)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::x::x_seller_offer_price"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p-market","symbol":"p^M","meaning":"Uniform local market price in the local uniform-price auction, treated as the given threshold in the buyer and seller allocation-permission conditions.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p-market"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p-bid-i","symbol":"p_i^{bid}","meaning":"Buyer i's submitted bid price in the local uniform-price auction, as referenced by the buyer acceptance threshold.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p-bid-i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p-offer-j","symbol":"p_j^{offer}","meaning":"Seller j's offered or selling price in the local uniform-price auction, as referenced by the seller acceptance threshold.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p-offer-j"},{"parameter_id":"p_market","symbol":"p^{market}","meaning":"Uniform local market price at which all accepted bids pay or receive the same price, used as the threshold in buyer and seller trading permissions.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::theta::p_market"},{"parameter_id":"theta_uniform_market_price","symbol":"p^{market}_{t}","meaning":"Uniform local market price ('this price') at time t; all accepted bids pay or receive the same market price, and the source elsewhere calls the demand-supply intersection the market closing price. Its value is determined by market clearing and is not specified by the R008 evidence.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"market clearing price (endogenous; value not specified in rule evidence)"},"unit":null,"indices":["t (auction time step)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e10"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_uniform_market_price"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","stage":"L6","subtype":"aggregate_bid_curve_intersection_price","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"With the Nash equilibrium dispatch as quantities and the supply and demand bids submitted by participants as prices, the MO forms increasing supply and decreasing demand step curves according to price priority order, and determines the MCP at the intersection of the two aggregate curves.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: aggregate supply and demand price-quantity curves","Core operation: aggregate by price sorting and take the intersection of supply and demand curves","Output: local market clearing price MCP"],"variation_fields":["Adopts a day-ahead forward double-sided auction","Curve quantities come from the equilibrium dispatch in Step 4","Curve prices come from the double-sided bids submitted by participants","The MCP is used for surplus-electricity trading and serves as the unit payment price at which the retailer purchases unsold surplus electricity"],"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C005","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001"],"paper_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","template_code":"DA"},{"unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","stage":"L6","subtype":"uniform_auction_clearing_price","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The local auction forms the market closing price at the intersection of supply and demand curves; all accepted bids in the same clearing round use the same unit electricity price.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: the unit market price of local electric energy trading","Core operation: a uniform clearing price is formed from the intersection of supply and demand curves","Output: a common price applicable to accepted buy and sell bids in the same round"],"variation_fields":["The uniform price varies with the clearing round and is communicated to each agent","The price is used for buy/sell permission thresholds and settlement of electric energy charges","The price increase driven by synchronized heat-pump demand bids in the transition season is a scenario observation reported","No detailed price-selection rule is given when the curve intersection is not unique"],"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C002","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C003","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013::v141-c-R013-C001"],"paper_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","source_definition":"With the Nash equilibrium dispatch as quantities and the supply and demand bids submitted by participants as prices, the MO forms increasing supply and decreasing demand step curves according to price priority order, and determines the MCP at the intersection of the two aggregate curves.","retained_variants":["Day-ahead forward double-sided auction, in which the MO calculates prices for H-MGs and retailers.","Quantities come from the Nash equilibrium optimal dispatch in Step 4; prices come from the supply and demand bids submitted by participants.","Aggregate supply and demand are monotonically increasing and decreasing step curves, respectively.","The MCP is used for surplus-electricity trading and calculation of participant revenues; the retailer purchases, at the MCP, surplus electricity not sold to other H-MGs."],"constraint_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C005","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001"]},{"unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","source_definition":"The local auction forms the market closing price at the intersection of supply and demand curves; all accepted bids in the same clearing round use the same unit electricity price.","retained_variants":["The MO organizes supply and demand bids with the objective of maximizing social welfare; this objective is not equated with the Nash-equilibrium quantity source of 33.","In the same clearing round, all accepted bids pay or receive the same market price; the price may vary across rounds.","The market price is communicated to each agent and used for settlement of electric energy charges; taxes, network charges, and deviation charges still belong to other cost components.","A buyer bid not below the market price and a seller bid not above the market price respectively constitute buy and sell permission conditions, and cannot replace the intersection-pricing definition.","The price increase driven by synchronized heat-pump demand bids is an observation for a specific scenario; no detailed price-selection rule is given for the case of a non-unique intersection."],"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C004","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C005","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C002","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C003","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R013::v141-c-R013-C001"]}],"source_parent_definition":{"definition":"In the local double-sided electric energy auction, supply offers are ordered ascending and demand offers descending to form supply and demand curves, and the price coordinate of the intersection determines the market clearing price.","object":"The supply-demand price-quantity curves of local electric energy trading and the market price corresponding to their intersection.","inputs":"Bids and corresponding quantities of buyer demand and seller supply; the sources of quantities and detailed curve-construction rules are retained in the respective members.","operation":"Sort separately by buyer and seller role to construct supply and demand curves, locate the intersection, and take its price coordinate.","outputs":"Local market clearing price; the applicable price scope of each member is retained separately.","boundary":"Limited to intersection pricing within L6 and the DA template. Quantity dispatch, optimization objectives, trading permission, price publication, and settlement do not become parent operations; no rules are added for the case where the intersection does not exist or is not unique, and the same-round uniform price commitment for all accepted buy and sell bids in 45 is not generalized to 33."},"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/169"});
